      "body": "Quick Answer\n\nThe Tunnel Escape Fates Entwined system requirements are published on the Steam store page for AppID 4285110. The store lists a single Windows minimum row covering operating system, processor, memory, graphics, DirectX, storage, and network. Recommended PC specifications and Steam Deck verification status are not announced as of 2026-09-30.\n\nWhat the Tunnel Escape Fates Entwined system requirements row lists\n\nThe Steam store System Requirements section for AppID 4285110 publishes a Windows minimum row. That row defines the categories a buyer must read to decide whether the Steam build will launch on a Windows machine. The categories published under the minimum row are:\n\n- Operating system\n- Processor\n- Memory\n- Graphics\n- DirectX\n- Storage\n- Network\n\nThe minimum row describes the smallest machine on which the developer (Elzee) confirms the build will run. The store page does not pair that row with a screen resolution, frame rate, or quality preset, so the minimum row should be read as a launch floor rather than as a recommended play setup.\n\nWhere the values come from\n\nEach category on the minimum row carries a specific value on the Steam store page. This guide treats the existence of those seven categories as confirmed current-game facts; the actual numeric values and tier wording live on the store page itself. If you are sizing a new machine or troubleshooting a low-spec PC, read the current values directly from the Steam listing, since Steam updates values without notice.\n\nWhy the minimum row is paired with a single-player restriction\n\nThe Steam store row labels the game as single-player only. The minimum row is sized for one running instance of the build and does not reserve headroom for a co-op or multiplayer session. If you plan to run the game alongside streaming, recording, voice chat, or background downloads, you should plan for additional headroom beyond the minimum values.\n\nRecommended PC specifications\n\nNot announced as of 2026-09-30. The Steam store page does not publish a separate Recommended row for Tunnel Escape Fates Entwined system requirements. Recommended specifications would change the answer if Elzee, Saikey Studios, or Valve publishes them on the store page, in an in-game settings menu, or in a Steam news update.\n\nSteam Deck verification status\n\nNot announced as of 2026-09-30. Steam Deck verification requires a developer build submission, after which Valve assigns one of four badges: Verified, Playable, Unsupported, or Unknown. The Tunnel Escape Fates Entwined store page does not currently show one of those four badges, so a buyer cannot rely on the Steam Deck label at this time. Steam Deck verification would change the answer once the developer or Valve publishes the badge on the store page.\n\nOther unannounced hardware rows\n\nNot announced as of 2026-09-30. The Steam store page does not publish a Mac row, a Linux row, a SteamOS row, or a console row. Those rows would change the answer if Elzee publishes them on the store page or in a Steam news update. The Windows minimum row is the only currently published hardware target."
